abstract: >-
  A deterministic, hand-checkable discrete-event simulator (Python 3 standard library
  only, no randomness) of a client's recovery layer after an ambiguous tool timeout,
  with a mock provider under two explicit contracts (no deduplication, and deduplication
  on a stable key), a lagging status endpoint, a webhook queue whose receipts can be
  delayed, duplicated, reordered, lost or misleading, and a private effect ledger used
  only for scoring. Sixteen scripted scenarios (17 operations) and 120 timing schedules
  score immediate retry, check-then-retry, wait-then-verify, defer-and-report and
  evidence reconciliation on duplicates, exactly-once completion, false completion,
  unresolved operations, retries and time to confirmation, with sensitivity, ablation
  and persistent-fault analyses. Includes a provider contract checklist, a decision
  table, and commands to run custom scenarios and policies or replay recorded
  observations.
